course: dictionary
lesson: 4659
title: Hoax: a trick that is not true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hoax is a trick. It makes lots of people believe something that is not true, such as a fake story, a fake picture or a fake warning. «Messages saying WhatsApp will start charging unless you forward them have been shared for years and are hoaxes.» The clue is in the words: they are tricks made up to fool people.
explain: To hoax people means to trick them in this way. «Such viral scares are usually hoaxes.» Viral means spreading fast online, so a hoax can travel very quickly. Check your meaning by swapping in "a trick that is not true" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some hoaxes are harmful. «Hoax 999 calls take time away from real emergencies and can lead to trouble with the police.» A hoax call wastes help that other people need, so it is a crime, not a joke.
explain: Before you believe or share something, wait for trusted news. «Wait for trusted news before believing or sharing that a famous person has died; celebrity death hoaxes are common.» Ask yourself: who made this, and can I check it somewhere trusted?
fact: Hoax is a noun (a hoax, hoaxes) and a verb (to hoax, hoaxing).
fact: «Hoax» means a trick that makes people believe something that is not true.
fact: «A hoax call» is a fake call, and «a hoax email» is a fake email.
fact: «It turned out to be a hoax» means it was found to be a trick.
fact: Hoaxes spread quickly online, so always check the source before you share.
exercise: «Such viral scares are usually hoaxes.» What is a hoax? | *A trick that makes people believe something untrue | A true news story from a trusted paper | A kind of sports match | A message from a best friend
exercise: What is a hoax call? | A call to wish someone happy birthday | *A fake call that wastes emergency help | A call to order a pizza | A call from a friend asking to play
exercise: Which word in «To hoax people means to trick them in this way» means to trick? | them | people | *hoax | means
test: «It turned out to be a hoax.» What does this mean? | It was the best day ever | It was a true and famous story | *It was a trick, not true | It was a gift from a friend
test: A shocking message says your town is in danger, and it is shared everywhere. What should you do first? | Ignore it and never think about it again | *Check it with trusted news before believing or sharing it | Call 999 to test if it is true | Share it with everyone quickly
exam: Why is a hoax 999 call wrong? | It is a fun game to play with friends | It is a kind joke that helps everyone | *It wastes help that real emergencies need, and it is a crime | It saves time for the emergency services
